  [SUPERSEDED] Network meta-analysis of CDK4/6 inhibitors (7 phase III RCTs, 4,415 patients, 73.3 months median follow-up)
     draft uses    : No statistically significant difference in OS between any pair of the three CDK4/6 inhibitors; 7 phase III RCTs, 4,415 patients, 73.3 months median follow-up
     latest known  : Scientific Reports, February 2024 (Comparative overall survival of CDK4/6 inhibitors in combination with endocrine therapy in advanced breast cancer). This is the paper the draft describes. However, its MONARCH 3 data input was the interim OS analysis (HR 0.754, 5.8 years follow-up), which has since been superseded by the final OS analysis (HR 0.804, 8.1 years, May 2024). A newer Lancet Oncology reconstructed individual patient data meta-analysis (Beshr et al., 2026) exists but addresses CDK4/6i vs endocrine therapy alone, not head-to-head drug comparisons.
     changes       : The NMA incorporated the MONARCH 3 interim OS HR of 0.754 (95% CI 0.584–0.974, 5.8 years follow-up) as its MONARCH 3 data point. The final MONARCH 3 OS analysis (May 2024, 8.1 years) gives HR 0.804 (95% CI 0.637–1.015). The point estimate and interval both shifted — the final HR is less favorable for abemaciclib and the CI now crosses 1.0 (non-significant), whereas the interim HR did not cross 1.0. The NMA's conclusion of no significant OS difference between drugs is directionally unchanged, but the underlying MONARCH 3 figure it used is now outdated. The draft does not itself quote the NMA's internal MONARCH 3 HR, so no draft figure is directly wrong, but the NMA it cites as evidence was built on superseded MONARCH 3 data.
     source        : https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-024-53151-8
     BEFORE ACTING : open the source above and read the sentence.

